# Feature workflow

1. Understand the requested behavior and acceptance criteria.
2. Localize the current implementation and relevant tests by searching before broad reading.
3. Assess callers, data flow, dependencies, and documentation impact.
{% if profile == "minimal" -%}
4. Identify the smallest owning module; introduce a new boundary only when the feature needs it.
{% else -%}
4. Identify the owning layer or domain before editing; preserve the **{{ profile }}** dependency
   direction.
{% endif -%}
5. Define verification before implementation.
6. Implement the minimum coherent change without speculative layers or dependencies.
7. Run the targeted behavior test, then the required repository gates.
8. Review the final diff for scope, ownership, and accidental changes.
